donald trump has made a lot of  investments over his career  one of the flashiest his purchase of  mar-a-lago also turned out to be one of  the best trump paid an estimated 10  million dollars for it in 1985 and  turned it into a money-making club  before a rising real estate market made  it one of the most valuable homes in the  world today the crown jewel of palm  beach is worth an estimated 350 million  dollars the property which was rated by  the fbi monday was historic long before  trump got involved with it  finished in 1927 mar-a-lago was given to  the federal government by the will of  the original owner serial heiress  marjorie merriweather post in hopes it  would be used as a presidential retreat  the government ultimately decided to  give mar-a-lago back to the marjorie  meriwether post foundation concerned  about maintenance and security in 1985  the foundation sold it to trump who paid  a reported 5 million dollars for the  house 3 million for the furniture and 2  million for the beachfront land across  the road  this was around the time trump started  to get ahead of himself and several of  his business deals in the 80s including  his 1988 purchase of new york city's  plaza hotel ended in bankruptcy by the  early 90s but luckily for trump he was  able to hang on to mar-a-lago  in 1995 he turned the mansion into a  private club hosting rich members and  glitzy events in 2015 trump declared he  was running for president and though his  comments on the campaign trail turned  off some customers others flocked to the  palm beach residence in 2014 mar-a-lago  generated an estimated 10 million  dollars a year in revenue the year trump  announced his presidential run sales  jumped to an estimated 22 million  dollars they climbed to an estimated 29  million dollars the following year after  winning the election trump reportedly  doubled the initiation fee to two  hundred thousand dollars as president he  took so many trips to the club that his  administration began referring to it as  the winter white house in some ways it  was the fulfillment of marjorie  merriweather post's dream but in 2017  trump's first year in the white house  revenues hit 25 million dollars they  trickled down to 23 million dollars in  2018 and 21 million dollars in 2019. by  the time covet 19 hit in 2020 forbes  estimated mar-a-lago was worth 170  million dollars  in typical fashion the trump  organization argued its value was closer  to 500 million then something remarkable  happened while many of trump's  businesses flailed about in the early  days of the pandemic mar-a-lago held on  with revenues landing at an estimated 23  million dollars in 2020.  at that point the real estate market  took off thanks to a flood of wealthy  northeasterners who rushed to palm beach  like never before  that 500 million dollar figure absurd at  the time that the trump organization  proposed it suddenly became somewhat  reasonable  real estate experts outside of palm  beach guessed that the place was worth  more than 200 million dollars  brokers on the island thought it'd be  worth far more with the most aggressive  estimate coming in at  725 million dollars  when forbes last valued the property in  march we went with a conservative 350  million dollars if trump sold mar-a-lago  for that amount he'd reap a 35 times  return on his original 10 million dollar  investment making it one of the best  deals of his career  [Music]
 

